        <headline>Wind Advisory issued September 25 at 11:09AM PDT until September 25 at 9:00PM PDT by NWS Spokane WA</headline>
        <description>* WHAT...Southwest winds around 20 to 30 mph with gusts up to 45 mph
expected.

* WHERE...Cloverland Road, Anatone, Badger Mountain Road, Spokane
Valley, Rosalia, Coulee City, Potlatch, Wilbur, Pomeroy, Alpowa
Summit, Creston, Downtown Spokane, Peola, Colfax, Mansfield, La
Crosse, Rockford, Grand Coulee, Moscow, Odessa, Harrington,
Ritzville, Plummer, Fairfield, Airway Heights, Clarkston, Pullman,
Cheney, Mountain Road, Uniontown, Davenport, Waterville, Tekoa,
Genesee, and Oakesdale.

* WHEN...Until 9 PM PDT this evening.

* IMPACTS...Gusty winds will blow around unsecured objects. Tree
limbs could be blown down and a few power outages may result.
Blowing dust may reduce visibility to less than one mile.
</description>
        <instruction>Winds this strong can make driving difficult, especially for high
profile vehicles. Use extra caution.</instruction>
